bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_any_typed_tuple_len_returns_minus_one_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch fix. inline_runtime_len_value takes a tuple_len func ref (rt_tuple_len, hosted targets only, declared as a codegen root); heap tag 4 calls it instead of answering -1. rt_tuple_len returns the arity for a Rust RuntimeTuple and -1 for a non-tuple, so a C-core enum (also tag 4) keeps -1. Strings, arrays and dicts keep the inline path. Red->green: compiler/tests/seed_jit_len_bound_proof_non_array.rs jit_tuple_len_through_any_and_untyped_parameter (a.len()*100 + count(t)*10 + count([1, 2]) gave -108, want 332). e2e on seed d844d70d90d3aa00: any / untyped tuple 3, dict 2, text 2, array 3, same as interpreter. Perf vs parent seed 20ce479a53519bab, 3 alternated rounds: untyped array+text len loop, 2e8 iterations, 6.77 vs 6.78 s mean, RSS 41 MB: no regression; a tuple len now costs one runtime call. Compiler lib: 12 origin failures + the order-dependent seed_builtin_discriminants_are_the_declared_ordinal."

